title: 'pallet-conviction-voting: make Tally::add and Tally::remove atomic'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `Tally::add` and `Tally::remove` assigned each field as it was computed, so a `checked_add` or
    `checked_sub` that failed part way through returned `None` with `support`, and sometimes `ayes`,
    already modified. Both now compute all three fields before assigning any of them, leaving the
    tally untouched when they return `None`.
crates:
- name: pallet-conviction-voting
  bump: patch
